From: Loïc Vigneron <loic@spin42.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: monaco-arduino-monza: Boot the MCU from its flash

GPIO 47 drives the STM32H5's BOOT0 through a level shifter. Left as an
input, the shifter holds BOOT0 high once the board is up, so any reset of
the MCU after power on, through NRST or its own, starts the ST ROM
bootloader instead of the application in flash. Hold it low.
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/monaco-arduino-monza.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/monaco-arduino-monza.dts
@@ -596,6 +596,17 @@
 	};
 
 	/*
+	 * The MCU's BOOT0, through a level shifter whose pull-ups would
+	 * otherwise hold it high: every MCU reset would start its ROM bootloader.
+	 */
+	mcu-boot0-hog {
+		gpio-hog;
+		gpios = <47 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		output-low;
+		line-name = "MCU_BOOT0";
+	};
+
+	/*
 	 * Tells the MCU's loader that Linux is up: it plays the boot animation
 	 * on the LED matrix and holds the sketch until this line is high.
 	 */
